        {
          "id": 2027701815,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "https://gitlab.com/wireshark/wireshark/-/merge_requests/16669#note_2026547985  \n> I don't have current (Qt 6.5.3) on dev system. Let me update and try again.  \n> Is there a CMake warning I'm missing about not being up to date?  \n  \nUpdating from 6.2.3 (which had been down graded from 6.2.4) to 6.5.3 was needed for the merge request above.  \n\nThe Windows build system lets me be lazy about checking versions by updating the libraries automatically when CMake is run. The one? package (Qt)  that's loaded manually leaves it up to me to have the proper version. It would be ok to change the message from a `FATAL_ERROR` to `WARNING` but if it can remind to do housekeeping it seems appropriate.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6701257,
            "username": "chuckcraft",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Chuck Craft",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/0809ffc6d9d98013a1895132bc055c622830b8a20bfa49328f53d5eb4a1206cb?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/chuckcraft"
          },
