        {
          "id": 2027365340,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Just an enquiry as my knowledge of Qt and CMake is a bit lacking.\n\nShould the version check be on Qt6 as a whole in `find_package`, i.e. can there be different versions of Qt6 and Widgets?\n\nAnd if the version check should be on the package, maybe an open-ended  version, e.g. `find_package(Qt6 6.5.3...< REQUIRED`.  I'm unsure how the version requirement should actually be expressed.\n\nAnd if none of the above is relevant, should the new check be condensed to `if ((WIN32 OR APPLE) AND Qt6Widgets_VERSION VERSION_LESS 6.5.3)`?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6621762,
            "username": "graham.bloice",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "Graham Bloice",
            "state": "active",
