        {
          "id": 2080832128,
          "type": "DiscussionNote",
          "body": "Officially, Qt has paid commercial support for Qt 5.15 for another 8 months (and 6.2 for another month.) The average person who is downloading the source code and compiling for Windows probably has some reason to do so instead of using the official packages, and I don't think it's wise to force exactly the same version that we're using for the official packages just because it's our official version.\n\nHowever, I would be fine with enforcing a minimum version on Windows (or macOS) that is similar to what is supported by Qt. In other words, we recommend and use the latest stable release, but I think we should only enforce that someone use a version supported by Qt. E.g., for the current master/5.0, we should be on 6.8.x when it releases, but it would probably be OK to allow 6.5.x.",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
            "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/johnthacker"
          },
