    {
      "id": "ab3173513fba705732c6d670746146b5cff0c4af",
      "individual_note": true,
      "resolvable": false,
      "notes": [
        {
          "id": 2027603603,
          "type": null,
          "body": "> Should the version check be on Qt6 as a whole in find_package, i.e. can there be different versions of Qt6 and Widgets?\n\nIt should be with `find_package` - Qt has been improving their [CMake support](https://doc.qt.io/qt-6/cmake-manual.html). There's some more modernization we could do at some point, and we could even modernize the Qt5 part, though we'll probably drop Qt5 before doing that.\n\nWhat's the reason for not letting people who are building with Windows or MacOS build with versions earlier than 6.5.3, though? Just to force people who are building from source (which is relatively rare on Windows and MacOS) to upgrade to whatever is used in the official packages?",
          "author": {
            "id": 6764551,
            "username": "johnthacker",
            "public_email": "",
            "name": "John Thacker",
            "state": "active",
            "locked": false,
            "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/99c30adacedf45514aaf711ba8a44f56322ebb53e9b550b7e3c9cd83bd6a1408?s=80&d=identicon",
